# Conductor — Hecksagon
#
# Persistence (i728 step 2 : make the implicit explicit, behavior-preserving).
# The Conductor context's aggregates (Claim, Lease, MergeQueue, Sweeper, Worker)
# hold the live merge-queue / worker-lease state and persist across boots today
# (information/conductor/{claim,lease,merge_queue,sweeper,worker}.heki round-trip).
# They reached heki via the implicit default ; :heki is declared here so the
# backing is EXPLICIT before the default flips to memory — without it the flip
# would silently drop the queue. Pairs with conductor.bluebook (+ entity files).
#
Hecks.hecksagon "Conductor" do
  adapter :heki
end
